    'pos.eyebrow':  'What is VLink',
    'pos.title':    'Built for <span class="grad">production-grade real-time</span> communication',
    'pos.sub':      'A C++17 communication middleware for autonomous driving and embodied AI. Compile-time template dispatch, an in-tree toolchain, portable across platforms — a complete real-time foundation from development through production.',
    'pos.c1.h':     'Full toolchain',
    'pos.c1.p':     'Viewer · Player · Analyzer desktop GUI · 10-piece CLI · Foxglove / Rerun web bridge · bag record/replay — develop, debug, and regress in one place.',
    'pos.c1.vs1':   'ROS2: rqt + bolt-on bridges',
    'pos.c1.vs2':   '<strong>VLink: in-tree</strong>',
    'pos.c2.h':     'Production-grade performance',
    'pos.c2.p':     'Shallow copy · stack-first allocation · lock-free queues · branch-prediction friendly — compile-time template dispatch, no vtable overhead; <code>intra://</code> sub-microsecond, <code>shm://</code> Iceoryx ~10 μs zero-copy.',
    'pos.c2.vs1':   'DDS cross-process ms-scale',
    'pos.c2.vs2':   '<strong>μs-scale zero-copy</strong>',
    'pos.c3.h':     'Auto-Dispatched Serialization',
    'pos.c3.p':     'Protobuf / FlatBuffers / CDR / POD / custom — selected at compile-time from your type signature. No hand-written codec.',
    'pos.c3.vs1':   'Msg / IDL / CDR fragmentation',
    'pos.c3.vs2':   '<strong>14 formats unified</strong>',
    'num.tr':       'Transports',
    'num.ser':      'Serializers',
    'num.cli':      'CLI Tools',
    'num.viz':      'GUI / Web Viz',

    'uni.eyebrow': 'Unified API',
    'uni.title':   'One API · <span class="grad">12 transports</span> · zero cognitive load',
    'uni.sub':     'The URL prefix <em>is</em> the transport selector — same business code, change the URL prefix to switch the backend.',
    'uni.mx.label': 'Transport Backends',
    'uni.mx.title': '12 transport backends · one-line URL switch',
    'uni.b1':      '<strong>Five lines to ship</strong> — from <code>#include</code> to <code>publish()</code> in under five lines; a newcomer has end-to-end Pub/Sub running in ten minutes.',
    'uni.b2':      '<strong>Zero cognitive load</strong> — no Node / Executor / Context scaffolding; one template class is one node, and the API shape stays identical across models.',
    'uni.b3':      '<strong>Protocol-agnostic</strong> — business code depends on no transport API; pick DDS, SHM, Zenoh or SOME/IP and the logic doesn&#39;t change.',
    'uni.b4':      '<strong>Seamless promotion</strong> — debug → prototype → production: only the URL prefix changes, the business code stays byte-for-byte the same.',

    'vs.eyebrow':  'VLink vs ROS2',
    'vs.title':    'Replace <span class="grad">ROS2</span> — lighter, faster, more modern',
    'vs.sub':      'VLink is not "yet another node library". It is a <strong>full real-time system platform</strong> for production vehicles and commercial robots — comms, visualization, recording, encryption, CLI and web, all in one.',
    'vs.dom.h':    'Supply chain &amp; compliance',
    'vs.dom.p':    'ROS2’s RMW layer is dominated by Fast-DDS, CycloneDDS and Connext — all driven by overseas organizations, with limited swap paths. VLink’s framework is Apache 2.0 and transport-agnostic at the URL layer: swap in CycloneDDS · QNX IPC · the Chinese <strong>TravoDDS</strong> or any other trusted stack to meet <strong>sovereign-tech &amp; compliance</strong> requirements.',

    'sc.eyebrow':   'Use Cases',
    'sc.title':     '<span class="grad">Four representative scenarios</span> · one API across them all',
    'sc.sub':       'From high-bandwidth camera and point-cloud pipelines in autonomy and robotics, to LAN-scale distributed communication, automotive Ethernet integration, and cross-network monitoring with Web visualization, VLink switches deployment shape through one node API plus different URL backends.',
    'sc.ad.tag':    'Autonomous Driving',
    'sc.ad.h':      'Multi-sensor perception pipelines',
    'sc.ad.p':      'The docs treat autonomous driving as a core target domain. For same-host large payloads such as images and point clouds, <code>shm://</code> is the recommended zero-copy path; for cross-machine distribution you can switch to <code>dds://</code> or <code>ddsc://</code> without changing business logic.',
    'sc.rb.tag':    'Robotics / Embodied',
    'sc.rb.h':      'Mixed control and perception links',
    'sc.rb.p':      'Robotics and embodied systems usually combine low-latency control loops with high-bandwidth perception streams. <code>intra://</code> fits in-process control paths, while same-host camera and point-cloud traffic can move to <code>shm://</code> under the same API surface.',
    'sc.soa.tag':   'Automotive Integration',
    'sc.soa.h':     'Automotive Ethernet with AUTOSAR alignment',
    'sc.soa.p':     'The docs explicitly position <code>someip://</code> as the Beta backend for automotive Ethernet and AUTOSAR-oriented integration, and provide a <code>someip_flat</code> example. During development you can still start with <code>dds://</code> or <code>intra://</code> and switch by URL later.',
    'sc.cl.tag':    'Cross-Network / Web',
    'sc.cl.h':      'Remote monitoring and cloud-edge access',
    'sc.cl.p':      'For cross-subnet, cross-VLAN, or browser-based visualization workflows, the docs offer two paths: <code>zenoh://</code> for NAT-crossing cloud-edge communication, and Proxy / WebViz for remote monitoring, data forwarding, and bridging into Foxglove Studio or Rerun Viewer.',

    'mdl.eyebrow':  'Three Models',
    'mdl.title':    'Three communication models · One mental model',
    'mdl.sub':      'Event / Method / Field — these three cover 99% of your needs, sharing a uniform API shape.',
    'mdl.event.h':  'Event Model',
    'mdl.event.d':  'Many-to-many async fan-out. Default choice for sensors, state broadcast, log streams.',
    'mdl.method.h': 'Method Model',
