    'hero.h1': 'One <span class="grad">API</span>,<br><span class="num">12</span> transports,<br><span class="grad">zero migration cost</span>',
    'vs.foot': '※ This table is a summary illustration; refer to each project&#39;s current docs and source for authoritative capabilities.',
    'vz.c.viewer': '<p class="viz-intro">A Qt6 desktop workbench for real-time monitoring and inspection of a VLink network.</p><ul><li>URL topic tree with live Freq / Rate / Loss / Latency columns</li><li>TrafficWidget waveforms over per-process QoS and a topology graph</li><li>Protobuf / FlatBuffers messages unfolded field-by-field, with <code>.proto</code> directories hot-loaded</li><li>OSG 3D point cloud with vehicle overlay, plus multi-stream camera tile (JPEG / H.264 / H.265 / NV12, software or hardware decoders)</li><li>Works offline too &mdash; open a <code>.vdb</code> SQLite file without any running middleware</li></ul>',
    'vz.c.webviz': '<p class="viz-intro">A long-running C++ bridge that feeds VLink data into Foxglove Studio and Rerun Viewer.</p><ul><li><code>vlink-foxglove</code>: WebSocket :8765, speaking Foxglove WS protocol v1</li><li><code>vlink-rerun</code>: gRPC :9876, with four run modes &mdash; spawn / connect / serve / save</li><li>7 built-in zero-copy container mappings (CameraFrame, PointCloud, OccupancyGrid, Tensor, ObjectArray, AudioFrame, RawData), plus shippable vlink_msgs example mappings</li><li>Reverse channel wired through: <code>clientPublish</code>, <code>Service Call</code>, and <code>Parameters</code> read/write</li><li>Built-in ExprTk for field remapping and unit conversion, with topic white / black-list filtering</li></ul>',
    'vz.c.player': '<p class="viz-intro">Frame-level bag replay &mdash; and a way to turn a recording back into live traffic.</p><ul><li><code>.vdb</code> / <code>.vdbx</code> (SQLite + LZAV) and <code>.vcap</code> / <code>.vcapx</code> (MCAP + Zstd, Foxglove-compatible) &mdash; both backends supported</li><li>Rate 0 – ∞×, step, loop, drag-seek, URL whitelist, <code>UrlRemap</code> renaming</li><li>Proxy mode launches <code>vlink-proxy</code> and republishes the bag as live traffic across the VLink network</li><li>Timeline IPC pipes the current timestamp to Analyzer so its cursor tracks playback in real time</li><li>Bag integrity check, index rebuild, and repair &mdash; all one click away</li></ul>',
    'vz.c.analyzer': '<p class="viz-intro">A QCustomPlot-based waveform workbench powered by the ExprTk expression engine.</p><ul><li>Three analysis modes: publish frequency, field value, and user-defined expression</li><li>ExprTk engine: arithmetic, trig, <code>sqrt</code> / <code>log</code> / <code>exp</code> / <code>abs</code>, plus user-defined variables</li><li>Seven line styles and ten number notations (Auto / Float 2,4,6,8 / Scientific 2,4,6,8 / Integer)</li><li>Dual mode: batch a whole bag offline, or follow Player live over the IPC time cursor</li><li>Dynamic Protobuf parsing, JSON preset switching, interruptible Progress, one-click PNG export</li></ul>',
